WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:03.629
♪♪

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:05.797
Claire Danes:
The Essex Serpent is a
beautifully written  

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:08.467
Claire Danes:
visceral and immediate story

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.470
Claire Danes:
about a victorian woman
Cora Seaborne.

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:17.392
She has recently widowed from a
very unhappy marriage.

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:20.646
You're free now Cora, to
explore.

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:24.274
Claire Danes:
Cora is kind of released into
the world and 

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:26.860
she gets to define for herself
who she is.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.364
Claire Danes:
She has a great passion for the
natural sciences.

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:36.078
And gets wind of a serpent
lurking in the Essex marshes

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.205
Claire Danes:
that really excites her
imagination.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:41.291
Claire Danes:
She decides to go investigate.

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:42.793
I've done some research.

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:43.961
Into a mythical beast?

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:45.712
Not mythical. Real!

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.464
♪♪

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:49.841
In Aldwinter, this rumour that
the Essex Serpent 

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.052
has returned is catching
like wildfire.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.304
Tom Hiddleston:
Something has been bumping into
the fishing boats.

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:56.556
Tom Hiddleston:
A teenage girl has gone missing.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:00.894
Tom Hiddleston:
The center of that community is
the local reverend

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.313
Tom Hiddleston:
Will Ransome, and his wife
Stella,

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:08.568
Tom Hiddleston:
and he is doing his best to
contain the anxiety of his parishioners.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:09.987
I told you.

00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:11.530
 I kept telling you we were in
danger.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.572
(Crowd roaring)

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.615
There is no Serpent!

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.659
♪♪

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.787
For Cora it's something that
does have a scientific

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:22.916
explanation and Will thinks it
doesn't really exist.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.129
Cora and Will begin an

00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:31.341
Tom Hiddleston:
intellectual and idealogical
debate about faith and reason.

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.553
Science requires dreams just
like your theology.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.221
Faith.

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:37.389
♪♪

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:42.561
Tom Hiddleston:
They have a deep mutual
admiration and a growing passion for each other

00:01:42.561 --> 00:01:44.646
which is destabilizing for both
of them.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.982
It was woman that was tempted by
the Serpent.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:48.984
It's the devil!

00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:50.277
♪♪

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:52.529
You let them accuse me. You said
nothing.

00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:53.447
I'm their pastor.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:55.824
So you can't be my friend and a
man of God?

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:58.452
I can't think clearly when I am
around you.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:00.037
♪♪

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:02.831
Claire Danes:
I think we make the mistake of
assuming

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:07.002
that the Victorian era was
stayed and repressed.

00:02:07.002 --> 00:02:14.301
Claire Danes:
I think it's subversive in how
we see our heroine who is kind of sturdy and intrepid. 

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:18.055
Certainly look different from
the woman I met in that grand
house.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.934
She is refusing to play the role
of the wife, the widow. 

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.271
Andrea Cornwell:
It's been fascinating trying to
break stereotypes. 

00:02:26.688 --> 00:02:30.692
Claire Danes:
It has a very contemporary and
fresh feeling.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.028
We live in times of
great change.

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:34.404
Exciting times! 

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:36.656
♪♪

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.951
There's a huge element of
mystery and supernatural to the
series,

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:44.748
Hayley Squires:
but it also has a very strong
human drive behind it.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:50.670
It sort of enlivens the past
with something very modern and
very real.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.508
So much of the story is about
love and fear. 

00:02:54.508 --> 00:02:57.135
Claire Danes:
Its unruliness and formidable
power. 

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:57.469
(Glass shatters)

00:02:57.469 --> 00:03:00.931
♪♪

